What changed in ChinUp
----------------------

WorkWell is an iOS application. ChinUp retargets it to macOS via Mac Catalyst
and reworks its behaviour. The significant differences:

  * Platform      Retargeted from iOS-only to macOS 15+ (Mac Catalyst),
                  including a floating desktop status widget and
                  Catalyst-specific audio, notification and lifecycle paths.

  * Thresholds    Replaced the single forward-tilt threshold with independent
                  lower and upper bounds, so both chin-down and chin-up
                  posture are detected, with a graduated warning zone between.

  * Reliability   Added AirPods removal and disconnection detection, with
                  configurable auto-pause and auto-resume, so alerts are no
                  longer emitted when the device is not being worn.

  * Correctness   Fixed the poor-posture percentage calculation.

  * Performance   Reduced CPU usage substantially: motion is polled on an
                  interval rather than driven by continuous callbacks, UI
                  state updates are suppressed while the window is not
                  visible, and background animations are opt-in.

  * Diagnostics   Added file-based logging.

  * Interface     Simplified the UI and removed unused controls.

